6. CUSTOMER CONSENT AND POLICY ACKNOWLEDGEMENT SYSTEM

Build a professional customer consent system across registration, pickup booking, shipment creation, quotation approval, payment and optional services.

The objective is to ensure customers understand the service they are requesting and the responsibilities of both parties.

Do not create meaningless consent buttons.

Each acknowledgement must explain the relevant policy in simple language.

Store an auditable record of each customer’s consent.

A. Account registration consent

During account creation, include:

Mandatory checkbox:

“I have read and agree to Swiftvero Express’s Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy.”

Provide clickable links to both policies.

Do not preselect the checkbox.

The customer must actively select it before account creation.

Record:

* Customer ID.
* Policy version.
* Date and time.
* Consent status.
* Relevant registration event.

B. Pickup booking consent

Before submitting a pickup request, display the following clearly separated acknowledgements.

Mandatory acknowledgement 1: Free pickup and paid shipping

“I understand that Swiftvero provides free pickup for eligible bookings, but international shipping and delivery are charged separately. Free pickup does not mean free delivery.”

Mandatory acknowledgement 2: 24-hour pickup commitment

“I understand that Swiftvero will arrange to collect my package within 24 hours after my successful pickup booking is confirmed. This commitment relates to collection, not international delivery.”

Mandatory acknowledgement 3: Facility weighing

“I understand that my package will not be weighed at my pickup address. Final inspection, preparation where necessary, measurements and weighing will take place at the appropriate Swiftvero facility.”

Mandatory acknowledgement 4: Accurate declaration

“I confirm that the information I provide about my package, its contents, quantity and declared value is accurate and complete.”

Mandatory acknowledgement 5: Restricted and prohibited goods

“I confirm that my package does not contain prohibited or restricted items unless they have been properly declared and expressly accepted by Swiftvero in accordance with applicable laws and shipping requirements.”

Provide a link to the Prohibited and Restricted Items Policy.

Mandatory acknowledgement 6: Package availability

“I agree to make my package available at the confirmed pickup address and provide accurate contact details and collection instructions.”

Mandatory acknowledgement 7: Contact and collection confirmation

“I authorize Swiftvero and its designated collection representatives to contact me about the pickup and coordinate collection of my package.”

Mandatory acknowledgement 8: Inspection and quotation

“I understand that Swiftvero will inspect and weigh my package at its facility and provide a final shipping quotation based on the confirmed shipment details before payment.”

Do not charge the final shipping amount before the quotation is approved.

Mandatory acknowledgement 9: Packaging and repackaging

“I understand that my package may require additional packaging or repackaging for safe transportation. Any chargeable packaging service must be explained to me and approved before the additional charge is applied.”

Do not advertise packaging as free unless Swiftvero has approved that policy.

Mandatory acknowledgement 10: Collection record

“I acknowledge that Swiftvero may record the package’s condition and collection details, including photographs, for identification, operational records and dispute resolution.”

Explain how such records are handled in the Privacy Policy.

Mandatory acknowledgement 11: Customer communication

“I agree to receive essential service communications about my booking, pickup, quotation, payment, shipment status and delivery.”

Distinguish essential transactional messages from promotional marketing.

Do not bundle marketing consent with mandatory service communication.

C. Quotation approval consent

Before the customer approves a quotation, display:

“I have reviewed the confirmed package weight, applicable shipping service, selected optional services and total amount payable. I approve this quotation and understand that payment is required before the shipment proceeds to the next applicable processing stage.”

Require active approval.

Record the quotation version, amount, customer ID and approval timestamp.

D. Cargo protection consent

If the customer selects cargo protection, display:

“I have reviewed the applicable cargo protection terms, eligibility, exclusions, declared value and compensation limits. I understand the conditions attached to this optional service.”

The customer must actively select the protection option.

Do not automatically add protection.

Do not falsely describe an unapproved protection arrangement as insurance.

Use only legally approved and provider-backed insurance terms where regulated insurance is offered.

E. Priority shipping consent

If Priority Shipping is selected, display:

“I understand that Priority Shipping attracts an additional fee and is subject to destination, shipment eligibility and service availability. I have reviewed the available estimated delivery information and agree to the additional charge.”

Do not promise an unsupported delivery date.

F. Payment acknowledgement

Before payment, display:

“I confirm that I have reviewed the final amount payable and authorize payment for the selected shipping service and optional services.”

Do not collect payment without displaying the final amount.

G. Marketing consent

Add a separate optional checkbox:

“I would like to receive Swiftvero promotional offers, shipping updates, discounts and marketing communications.”

This checkbox must:

* Be optional.
* Be unchecked by default.
* Be separate from mandatory service communications.
* Allow the customer to unsubscribe later.

H. Consent management

Build a consent record system that stores:

* Customer ID.
* Shipment ID or booking ID where applicable.
* Consent category.
* Exact policy or consent text version.
* Accepted or declined status.
* Date and time.
* User or staff action where applicable.
* Relevant audit information.

Do not store only a single general consent flag.

Do not allow staff to silently accept policies on behalf of customers.

If a staff member assists a walk-in customer, the customer must be able to review and acknowledge the applicable terms through a customer-facing screen, digital signature or documented approved alternative.

Consent records must be protected against unauthorized modification.

Where a policy changes materially, require renewed acknowledgement when appropriate.

